### To test these endpoints, first make sure you have a local MongoDB instance running at 127.0.0.1:27017

### 1. Create a user (POST)
# @name createUser
POST http://localhost:5002/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Jane Doe",
    "email": "jane@example.com",
    "age": 28
}

###

### 2. Get all users (GET)
GET http://localhost:5002/api/users

###

### 3. Replace {id} with the actual _id string returned from Step 1

### Update a user (PUT)
PUT http://localhost:5002/api/users/{id}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Jane Smith",
    "age": 29
}

###

### Get a single user by ID (GET)
GET http://localhost:5002/api/users/{id}

###

### Delete a user (DELETE)
DELETE http://localhost:5002/api/users/{id}

